# Non-prefixed entries in the source state would be copied into $HOME.
# Everything below is repository tooling/documentation, not dotfiles.

# Cloud tool config and credentials are machine-specific and interactive
# (aws configure, az login). Never manage — or publish — anything here.
.aws
.azure

# Context7 credentials stay local, including the old CLI credential store.
.config/context7
.config/context7/**

# VS Code: only the declarative files are managed, via explicit source paths:
#   private_dot_config/Code/User/{settings.json,mcp.json.tmpl}
#   dot_vscode/argv.json.tmpl
# The rest of ~/.config/Code/User and ~/.vscode is machine state and must
# never be `chezmoi add`ed wholesale: globalStorage/, workspaceStorage/, History/, mcp/,
# profiles/, state.vscdb*, storage.json, ~/.vscode/extensions/ and
# ~/.vscode-shared/ (state.vscdb can hold OAuth tokens). Comments only here —
# a `.vscode` pattern would also hide the managed dot_vscode/ file above.
# The Kilo MCP modify template manages only its Context7 entry in globalStorage.

